                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make low clicking sounds (refers to hens)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df4bc21e-ebe9-458e-823b-8ce4aeb3c0e2",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4a935d-5e95-3819-9678-1aba3ff411eb",
                                                "text": "\"I came across him once,\" he continued, \"when he was playing down on the main road to Skaug; there he sat in the middle of the road with a lot of hens around him, I counted seven, and there were more round about in the wood, for I heard them clucking and calling behind every bush.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be8c66f9-f056-387b-b11f-235c8a35e7b4",
                                        "entry_id": "50c14512-6fbe-374a-a61c-3e4f40cad8b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause (the tongue) to make a clicking sound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b18f835-2fd7-4193-8c39-73d7ef1f7a09",
                                                "sense_id": "be8c66f9-f056-387b-b11f-235c8a35e7b4",
                                                "text": "My mother clucked her tongue in disapproval."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7eae1f2-75fe-3c5a-89ed-ea8958617dca",
                                        "entry_id": "50c14512-6fbe-374a-a61c-3e4f40cad8b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To call together, or call to follow, as a hen does her chickens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2516fb0a-4202-4655-b86c-c88ae95ce448",
                                                "sense_id": "a7eae1f2-75fe-3c5a-89ed-ea8958617dca",
                                                "text": "When she, poor hen, fond of no second brood,\nHas clucked thee to the wars and safely home."
